  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\n\nAn H5 longwave will move from the Pacific Coast toward the \nIntermountain West early Saturday. The wave weakens by the time it \ncrosses the Rockies, with a more compact wave taking shape and \nejecting toward the Central and Southern Plains areas late Saturday \ninto Sunday. The majority of model guidance suggests precip \ntied to the disturbance staying to our southwest. LREF guidance \nshows anywhere from 5 to 15% chance for any precip clipping us, \nprimarily across our far southwest areas. This is in good\nagreement with the latest NBM run which has trended noticeably \ndrier too as less than 10% PoPs are forecast for that \naforementioned area on Sunday. Highs this weekend remain the \n40s.\n\nFor the upcoming week, will see H5 ridging overspread much of the \ncentral CONUS. Expanding thicknesses should lead to a warming trend \nthrough Wednesday as highs return to the 50s and low 60s. Dry \nconditions will prevail through at least late Tuesday. Thereafter, \nmodels suggest an H5 wave ejecting from the Rockies toward the \nNorthern Plains. There are still differences apparent with the \ntiming and location of the wave, but for now, NBM depicts our area \nwith a 20 to 40% chance for some rain.",
